  "question": {
    "text": "In a YDSE bi-chromatic light of wavelengths,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>560</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> are used. The distance between the plane of the slits is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1&nbsp;</mn><mi>mm</mi></math> and the distance between the slits and the screen is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The minimum distance between two successive regions of complete darkness is"
  },
